// Title: Suspicious Regsvr32 Execution From Remote Share
// Sigma ID: 88a87a10-384b-4ad7-8871-2f9bf9259ce5
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-10-31 | Modified: 2026-10-18
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.010
// Description: Detects REGSVR32.exe to execute DLL hosted on remote shares. This could be an indicator of
//   threat actor abusing regsvr32 to download and install DLLs located remotely on a network share
//   of threat actor infrastructure.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2022/10/31/follina-exploit-leads-to-domain-compromise/
//   - https://www.cyberproof.com/blog/beyond-powershell-analyzing-the-multi-action-clickfix-variant/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/fba4b94a2237d0ec8fe1cd5dc9c4c29dc6d3e4c4/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_regsvr32_remote_share.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "\\REGSVR32.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " \\\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains " \"\\\\")
